{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1778 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "91e5c226ab06f0002f147b2720e7adcd885675f71bcd19eaf91f70ebeec97dda" :edb/db-before-t 1777 :edb/db-after-t 1778 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535090 50 #inst "2026-10-08T16:39:42.352Z" 13194139535090 true] [17592186119756 1020 #edb/ref 17592186330664 13194139535090 true] [17592186119757 1020 #edb/ref 17592186330678 13194139535090 true] [17592186119758 1020 #edb/ref 17592186330657 13194139535090 true] [17592186119758 1020 #edb/ref 17592186330685 13194139535090 true] [17592186119759 1020 #edb/ref 17592186330671 13194139535090 true] [17592186330657 1017 #edb/ref 17592186330658 13194139535090 true] [17592186330657 1089 "q-128383" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330657 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535090 true] [17592186330657 1100 "Given the Cartesian equation $5y-z+17=0$ of the plane $Π$, find an equation of $Π$ in the form $(r-p)\\cdot n=0.$" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330657 1113 #uuid "6aa44b3e-f639-568d-9d5b-c3b1165a65d8" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330657 1145 "First, from the equation of the plane we get that the normal vector of $Π$ is $n=⟨0,5,-1⟩.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $Π$ for $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5y-z+17 & =0 \\\\ z & =5y+17.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put, say, $y=0$, we get $z=17.$ Hence, the point $P(0,0,17)$ lies on $Π.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,0,17⟩.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-⟨0,0,17⟩)\\cdot ⟨0,5,-1⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330658 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330659 13194139535090 true] [17592186330658 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330660 13194139535090 true] [17592186330658 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330661 13194139535090 true] [17592186330658 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330662 13194139535090 true] [17592186330658 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330663 13194139535090 true] [17592186330658 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535090 true] [17592186330658 1041 "selection" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330658 1104 #edb/ref 17592186330659 13194139535090 true] [17592186330658 1110 #uuid "02fbfa6a-5308-5cf2-b9f7-b31ea8236a63" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330659 1034 "(r-⟨0,0,17⟩)\\cdot ⟨0,5,-1⟩=0" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330659 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535090 true] [17592186330659 1111 #uuid "6f6c7545-300a-5f79-9ad5-7f782ed66287" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330660 1034 "(r-⟨0,0,-15⟩)\\cdot ⟨-1,5,0⟩=0" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330660 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535090 true] [17592186330660 1111 #uuid "7612117a-0b40-5aca-a74d-7b61bd70081a" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330661 1034 "(r-⟨0,0,-21⟩)\\cdot ⟨5,0,-1⟩=0" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330661 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535090 true] [17592186330661 1111 #uuid "f7906bff-53ba-5d37-a117-b6295b92ec3c" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330662 1034 "(r-⟨0,0,13⟩)\\cdot ⟨0,-1,5⟩=0" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330662 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535090 true] [17592186330662 1111 #uuid "aa61c838-b3e4-5a91-adcd-a4b5442e3c76" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330663 1034 "(r-⟨0,0,11⟩)\\cdot ⟨0,5,1⟩=0" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330663 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535090 true] [17592186330663 1111 #uuid "7b76d532-b19d-53d8-af16-cf5c45f7d481" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330664 1017 #edb/ref 17592186330665 13194139535090 true] [17592186330664 1089 "q-330500" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330664 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535090 true] [17592186330664 1100 "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(2,1,-5)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=⟨6,-2,0⟩.$" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330664 1113 #uuid "e5f496f5-82da-5347-a9dc-1d7749662c5b" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330664 1145 "First, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=⟨2,1,-5⟩$ and the normal vector of the plane is $n=⟨6,-2,0⟩.$\n\nUsing the dot product we can find an equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨6,-2,0⟩ & =⟨2,1,-5⟩\\cdot ⟨6,-2,0⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨6,-2,0⟩ & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨6,-2,0⟩ & =10 \\\\ 6x-2y & =10 \\\\ 6x-2y-10 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330665 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330666 13194139535090 true] [17592186330665 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330667 13194139535090 true] [17592186330665 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330668 13194139535090 true] [17592186330665 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330669 13194139535090 true] [17592186330665 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330670 13194139535090 true] [17592186330665 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535090 true] [17592186330665 1041 "selection" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330665 1104 #edb/ref 17592186330668 13194139535090 true] [17592186330665 1110 #uuid "d3f8355a-f47d-5fde-944c-7f01b71f1f6e" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330666 1034 "6x+y-10=0" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330666 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535090 true] [17592186330666 1111 #uuid "4b2bacdd-6cb8-50d4-8afa-5d4d7bc3e608" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330667 1034 "x-6y-10=0" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330667 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535090 true] [17592186330667 1111 #uuid "65efd500-d89f-5b07-ae17-7ca8d5c2fe7a" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330668 1034 "6x-2y-10=0" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330668 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535090 true] [17592186330668 1111 #uuid "ff97a1c2-3ba8-50b5-9630-7c229350dc78" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330669 1034 "6x-2y+z-10=0" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330669 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535090 true] [17592186330669 1111 #uuid "b30c4d34-7509-5372-aa3a-3f0d318eaf69" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330670 1034 "6x-y-10z=0" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330670 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535090 true] [17592186330670 1111 #uuid "12a26a86-a380-5d97-8b3e-f14defa24e02" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330671 1017 #edb/ref 17592186330672 13194139535090 true] [17592186330671 1017 #edb/ref 17592186330674 13194139535090 true] [17592186330671 1017 #edb/ref 17592186330676 13194139535090 true] [17592186330671 1089 "q-336358" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330671 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535090 true] [17592186330671 1100 "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(-4,3,5)$ and is parallel to the vectors ${v}_{1}=⟨2,-3,-6⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨0,2,-8⟩.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$x\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$y\\,+\\,z\\,+$\n{{field-3}}\n$=0$" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330671 1113 #uuid "bc0bcd5d-4d1d-5e96-9f96-539ff833a355" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330671 1145 "First, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=⟨-4,3,5⟩.$\n\nNow, we need to find the normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={v}_{1}\\times {v}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -3 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -8\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =36i+16j+4k \\\\  & =⟨36,16,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨36,16,4⟩ & =⟨-4,3,5⟩\\cdot ⟨36,16,4⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨36,16,4⟩ & =-76\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨36,16,4⟩ & =-76 \\\\ 36x+16y+4z & =-76 \\\\ 36x+16y+4z+76 & =0 \\\\ 9x+4y+z+19 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330672 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330673 13194139535090 true] [17592186330672 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535090 true] [17592186330672 1041 "field-1" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330672 1104 #edb/ref 17592186330673 13194139535090 true] [17592186330672 1110 #uuid "18d0d219-ec4f-53bb-97f0-b1c5bd529520" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330673 1034 "9" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330673 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535090 true] [17592186330673 1111 #uuid "f7d4c5e8-f936-53a9-bc5f-3cca97c3b2c0" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330674 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330675 13194139535090 true] [17592186330674 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535090 true] [17592186330674 1041 "field-2" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330674 1104 #edb/ref 17592186330675 13194139535090 true] [17592186330674 1110 #uuid "842469ef-6b3f-52d4-b990-df6cd1e2c154" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330675 1034 "4" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330675 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535090 true] [17592186330675 1111 #uuid "3f369a1e-a1c1-580a-b60d-5664c6315eb4" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330676 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330677 13194139535090 true] [17592186330676 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535090 true] [17592186330676 1041 "field-3" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330676 1104 #edb/ref 17592186330677 13194139535090 true] [17592186330676 1110 #uuid "c362e1f6-816b-5c65-bc37-a382d6255263" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330677 1034 "19" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330677 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535090 true] [17592186330677 1111 #uuid "c637def1-cd89-5a2f-83b5-1ab8c3027aad" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330678 1017 #edb/ref 17592186330679 13194139535090 true] [17592186330678 1089 "q-336407" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330678 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535090 true] [17592186330678 1100 "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(2,-3,1)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n$r=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330678 1113 #uuid "d501cbc7-e6c3-5ee6-bf3b-290a3eeec39d" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330678 1145 "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨2,-3,1⟩.$ From the vectorial equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨4,0,-2⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is\n\n$$\nn=⟨4,0,-2⟩,\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,0,-2⟩ & =⟨2,-3,1⟩\\cdot ⟨4,0,-2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,0,-2⟩ & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute  $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨4,0,-2⟩ & =3 \\\\ 4x-2z & =6 \\\\ 4x-2z-6 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330679 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330680 13194139535090 true] [17592186330679 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330681 13194139535090 true] [17592186330679 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330682 13194139535090 true] [17592186330679 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330683 13194139535090 true] [17592186330679 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330684 13194139535090 true] [17592186330679 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535090 true] [17592186330679 1041 "selection" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330679 1104 #edb/ref 17592186330683 13194139535090 true] [17592186330679 1110 #uuid "4538f7fa-876c-5ec8-825c-2a661cb26038" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330680 1034 "4x+y-2z-5=0" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330680 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535090 true] [17592186330680 1111 #uuid "7ba28ff5-ac52-516d-924d-c3aac3509bb4" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330681 1034 "3x+y-2z-3=0" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330681 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535090 true] [17592186330681 1111 #uuid "4d7bf099-5abd-5ebb-b7b8-f635a931e376" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330682 1034 "4x+y+2z-3=0" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330682 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535090 true] [17592186330682 1111 #uuid "5a938bfe-8aab-5fb8-b67e-43d647955b92" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330683 1034 "4x-2z-6=0" 13194139535090 true] [17592186330683 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535090 true] [17592186330683 1111 #uuid "615827cd-5